          "thm-measurability-of-integration-against-a-kernel",
          "def-product-measure-on-sigma-finite-spaces",
          "thm-sigma-finite-product-measure-exists-is-rectangular-and-is-unique",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "thm-ftc-second-part",
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "def-feature-measure-energy",
          "thm-heine-borel-rn",
          "cor-arzela-ascoli-subsequence-theorem-for-proper-metric-targets",
          "thm-fundamental-theorem-of-calculus-for-absolutely-continuous-functions",
          "thm-lipschitz-characterisation-within-absolutely-continuous-functions"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "local_order": 12,
        "justified_by": [],
      "statement": "Assume AC and the feature-measure energy hypotheses. Fix $r>0$ and a nonempty closed convex constraint $D\\subseteq\\Omega$. For every continuous moment path $m:[0,T]\\to\\mathcal H$, the nonautonomous inclusion\n$$\\dot X(t)\\in-\\partial_{\\lambda_V}(V+\\iota_D)(X(t))-d\\Phi_{X(t)}^*\\nabla R(m(t))$$\nhas a unique forward solution from each $X(0)\\in D\\cap Q_r$; its characteristic map is jointly continuous in $(t,X(0))$ and locally Lipschitz in the initial point on each $Q_r$. Let $\\mu_t$ and $\\nu_t$ be two finite-action solutions on $[0,T]$ of the continuity equation with laws concentrated on $D\\cap Q_r$ and velocities\n$$v_t^\\alpha(x)=-\\operatorname{argmin}\\{|q|:q\\in d\\Phi_x^*\\nabla R(m_{\\alpha_t})+\\partial_{\\lambda_V}(V+\\iota_D)(x)\\},\\qquad\\alpha\\in\\{\\mu,\\nu\\},$$\nwhere $m_\\alpha=\\int\\Phi\\,d\\alpha$. The full shifted minimum selection is Borel; it need not be continuous in position. Each finite-action PDE solution with a continuous prescribed feature moment is the pushforward by its unique characteristic map. For starts in $D\\cap Q_r$, these characteristics remain in a larger $Q_R$ uniformly on compact time intervals, and their velocity is the negative full shifted minimum almost everywhere. The same construction applies directly to any continuous forcing $a(t)\\in\\mathcal H$ in place of $\\nabla R(m(t))$. Then for all $t\\in[0,T]$,\n$$W_2(\\mu_t,\\nu_t)\\le e^{(C_r-\\lambda_V)t}W_2(\\mu_0,\\nu_0),\\qquad C_r=L_rA_r^2+N_rB_r.$$\nHere $A_r=\\sup_{Q_r}\\|d\\Phi\\|$, $B_r=\\operatorname{Lip}_{Q_r}(d\\Phi)$, $M_r=\\sup_{Q_r}\\|\\partial V\\|$ in the bounded-selection convention, and $L_r,N_r$ are respectively a Lipschitz constant and a norm bound for $dR$ on the closed convex hull of $\\Phi(Q_r)$. In particular, the localized measure-valued flow is unique for each initial law. The estimate does not assume that $v_t$ is continuous in position.\n\n"
      },
