        "justified_by": [],
      "statement": "Assume AC and the feature-measure energy hypotheses. Let $\\mu_0\\in\\mathcal P_2(\\Omega)$ have finite energy and be concentrated on $Q_r$, and let $X:[0,\\infty)\\to K=L^2(\\mu_0;\\mathbb R^d)$ be the Hilbert gradient flow of the localized lift $E_r$ from $X(0,s)=s$. Define $\\mu_t=(X(t,\\cdot))_\\#\\mu_0$, $m_t=\\int\\Phi(X(t,s))d\\mu_0(s)$, and\n$$v_t(u)=-S(\\nabla R(m_t),u),$$\nwhere $S(a,u)$ is the minimum-norm element of the full shifted set $d\\Phi_u^*a+\\partial_{\\lambda_V}(V+\\iota_{Q_r})(u)$ for $u\\in Q_r$, and extend $v_t$ by $0$ for $u\\notin Q_r$. Then $v$ is Borel, $\\int_0^T\\int|v_t|^2d\\mu_tdt<\\infty$ for each $T<\\infty$, and $\\partial_t\\mu_t+\\nabla\\cdot(v_t\\mu_t)=0$ in distributions on $(0,T)\\times\\mathbb R^d$. The curve $\\mu_t$ is in $AC^2([0,T];\\mathcal P_2(\\mathbb R^d),W_2)$, and $v$ is the minimum-action velocity, satisfying $\\int_0^T\\int|v_t|^2d\\mu_tdt=\\int_0^T|\\dot\\mu_t|_{W_2}^2dt$.\n\n"
